# Agent Fleet — shared site configuration
#
# Single place to point the fleet at your own infrastructure (model gateway,
# Opik, package mirrors, container image). Most lines are commented out and
# ship with a public-safe placeholder or default. Package mirror defaults
# are uncommented below — override in config.local.env if needed.
#
# This committed template is sourced by the Harbor runner
# (Agents/utils/common/Harbor/env.sh), the OpenClaw setup
# (Agents/Openclaw/scripts/setup.sh), and the PinchBench and clawBio runners.
# An adjacent config.local.env
# (git-ignored) is sourced right after this file and overrides it. Uncommented
# values here override the built-in defaults; to override for a single run, pass
# an environment variable instead.
#
# Keep real secrets out of this committed file: put credentials (API_KEY)
# in config.local.env, or export them in your shell.

# ── Model gateway ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OpenAI- or Anthropic-compatible endpoint and credential. BASE_URL is the API
# root WITHOUT a version suffix; the runners append /v1 (or /v1/chat/completions)
# as needed, so a URL already ending in /v1 also works.
# BASE_URL=https://api.example.com
# API_KEY=sk-your-key
# MODEL=your-model-id
# Harbor fixed-run generation controls. Temperature and top_p require
# AGENT=opencode; max tokens also applies to Claude Code and Pi.
# HARBOR_TEMPERATURE=0.2
# HARBOR_TOP_P=0.9
# HARBOR_MAX_TOKENS=8192
# Pi task-container runtime. The package matches the control-plane Pi installed
# by scripts/setup.sh. PI_PROVIDER is optional: when unset it is derived from
# the BASE_URL host instead of a hard-coded placeholder name.
# PI_VERSION=0.81.1
# PI_PROVIDER=my-gateway
# PI_THINKING_LEVEL=high

# Harbor Fixer overrides. Shared BASE_URL, API_KEY, and MODEL remain the
# fallback; keep real credentials in config.local.env.
# HARBOR_FIXER_BASE_URL=https://api.example.com/v1
# HARBOR_FIXER_API_KEY=sk-your-key
# HARBOR_FIXER_MODEL=your-model-id
# HARBOR_FIXER_PI_BIN=pi
# HARBOR_FIXER_PI_PROVIDER=harbor-fixer
# HARBOR_FIXER_NO_PROXY=0
# HARBOR_FIXER_AGENT_TIMEOUT=900
# HARBOR_FIXER_EXECUTION_TIMEOUT=300
# HARBOR_FIXER_SUMMARY_LIMIT=4000
# HARBOR_FIXER_MAX_CONCURRENCY=4
# HARBOR_FIXER_MAX_TASK_SUMMARY_CHARS=24000
# HARBOR_FIXER_MAX_TASK_SUMMARIES_CHARS=400000

# ── qz (SII Inspire) E2B-compatible sandbox ──────────────────────────────────
# Set RL_ENVIRONMENT_TYPE=qz to run Harbor trials in qz sandboxes
# (https://qz-sbx-api.sii.edu.cn, an E2B-compatible control plane). The
# adapter (Agents/utils/common/Harbor/qz_e2b_sandbox.py) maps these onto the
# official e2b SDK. In a qz process, QZ_SANDBOX_*/SBX_* connection values
# override ambient cloud-E2B settings; E2B_API_KEY is only a fallback when no
# qz key is configured and its value is an sbx_-prefixed qz key. Keep the real
# key in config.local.env.
# RL_ENVIRONMENT_TYPE=qz
# SBX_API_KEY=sbx-your-key
# SBX_API_URL=https://qz-sbx-api.sii.edu.cn
# Select exactly one mode: a fixed platform Template for every trial, or a
# schema-v1 mapping that resolves each task to its own ready Template ID.
# QZ_SANDBOX_TEMPLATE=your_registered_template
# QZ_SANDBOX_TEMPLATE_MAP=/absolute/path/to/qz-templates.json
# Per-sandbox lifetime; the platform caps it at 4 hours (14400).
# QZ_SANDBOX_TIMEOUT_SEC=14400
# Real-agent runtime sources default to npmmirror on qz. Override the npm
# source with the shared NPM_CONFIG_REGISTRY setting below when needed.
# QZ_NODE_DIST_URL=https://nodejs.org/dist/v22.14.0/node-v22.14.0-linux-x64.tar.gz

# ── YiCloud OpenSandbox task images ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Set RL_ENVIRONMENT_TYPE=opensandbox to enable the YiCloud provider. When an
# explicit HARBOR_OPENSANDBOX_IMAGE_REF is absent, the Harbor runner builds the one
# selected local task, publishes a content-addressed image, and reuses its tag.
# Registry credentials stay in ~/.docker/config.json after `docker login`.
# RL_ENVIRONMENT_TYPE=opensandbox
# Optional trusted model-request customization for rollout agents. Version 1
# supports headers.set. Keep deployment values in config.local.env; /run_trial
# requests cannot supply or override this configuration.
# MODEL_REQUEST_CONFIG_JSON={"version":1,"headers":{"set":{"X-Route-Key":"deployment-a"}}}
# Every Sandbox must belong to an explicit environment. Prefer the immutable
# environment ID in automation; the exact name is resolved and cross-checked
# when only the name is available.
# YICLOUD_SANDBOX_ENVIRONMENT_ID=env-xxxxxxxx-xxx
# YICLOUD_SANDBOX_ENVIRONMENT_NAME=your-sandbox-environment
# Match the current YiCloud prewarm-pool flavor. Harbor task.toml resource
# requests are not forwarded because a different flavor takes the cold path.
# YICLOUD_SANDBOX_CPU=2
# YICLOUD_SANDBOX_MEMORY=8Gi
# YICLOUD_SANDBOX_LIFECYCLE_MINUTES=120
# Scheduling readiness is separate from Harbor's wider environment/agent setup
# ceiling. Pending state and platform reason are logged at the interval below.
# YICLOUD_SANDBOX_READY_TIMEOUT_SEC=300
# YICLOUD_SANDBOX_STATUS_LOG_INTERVAL_SEC=30
# Debug only: retain a Sandbox when environment start fails so the provider can
# inspect it. The log prints its ID; delete it manually after investigation.
# YICLOUD_SANDBOX_RETAIN_ON_START_FAILURE=0
# Debug only: retain a successfully completed trial's Sandbox until its platform
# lifecycle expires. Do not enable this for normal batch runs.
# YICLOUD_SANDBOX_RETAIN_AFTER_TRIAL=0
# The generic provider default remains HTTP. The YiCloud H launcher overrides
# it to S3: H publishes immutable objects and each Sandbox receives only a
# short-lived download URL plus the expected size and SHA-256.
# YICLOUD_SANDBOX_UPLOAD_BACKEND=http
# YICLOUD_SANDBOX_S3_CONFIG=/run/secrets/yicloud-s3cfg
# YICLOUD_SANDBOX_S3_BUCKET=bucket-cache
# YICLOUD_SANDBOX_S3_PREFIX=agent-fleet-upload/v1
# YICLOUD_SANDBOX_S3_CACHE_ROOT=/data/harbor-runs/opensandbox-s3-cache
# YICLOUD_SANDBOX_S3_LOCK_ROOT=/data/harbor-runs/opensandbox-s3-locks
# YICLOUD_SANDBOX_S3_SIGNED_URL_TTL_SEC=3600
# YICLOUD_SANDBOX_S3_DOWNLOAD_TIMEOUT_SEC=1800
# YICLOUD_SANDBOX_S3_DIRECTORY_COMPRESSION=auto
# YICLOUD_SANDBOX_S3CMD=s3cmd
# Explicit HTTP rollback path supplied by the Sandbox service.
YICLOUD_SANDBOX_FAST_UPLOAD_ORIGIN=https://sandbox.yicloud.com.cn
# YICLOUD_SANDBOX_UPLOAD_TIMEOUT_SEC=1800
# Keep the real project name in config.local.env. The image repository defaults
# to ${YICLOUD_PROJECT_NAME}/syslab-benchmark-task-images when it is set.
# YICLOUD_PROJECT_NAME=your-project
# HARBOR_OPENSANDBOX_IMAGE_REPOSITORY=your-project/syslab-benchmark-task-images
# HARBOR_OPENSANDBOX_SANDBOX_IMAGE_PREFIX=your-project/syslab-benchmark-task-images
# HARBOR_OPENSANDBOX_REGISTRY=registry.gate.yicloud.com.cn
# HARBOR_OPENSANDBOX_IMAGE_CACHE_ROOT=/data/harbor-runs/opensandbox-images
# HARBOR_OPENSANDBOX_IMAGE_PLATFORM=linux/amd64
# HARBOR_OPENSANDBOX_DOCKERHUB_MIRROR_PREFIX=m.daocloud.io/docker.io
# HTTP allows minimal base images without CA certificates to bootstrap APT;
# Release-file signatures still provide package metadata integrity checking.
# HARBOR_OPENSANDBOX_APT_MIRROR=http://mirrors.tuna.tsinghua.edu.cn
# HARBOR_OPENSANDBOX_BUILD_ARGS_JSON={}
# Keep this disabled for domestic-source-first builds. After explicitly running
# proxy_on as a fallback, set it to 1 to pass proxy variables into Docker build.
# HARBOR_OPENSANDBOX_BUILD_USE_PROXY=0

# ── Opik (optional) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# setup.sh asks for this endpoint and persists whether Opik should be used.
# OPIK_URL=https://opik.example.com/api
# OPIK_PROJECT_NAME=

# ── Package mirrors ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Override these to use private or regional mirrors. When unset, Harbor uses
# npmmirror for qz and npmjs for its other backends; standalone subsystems keep
# their own defaults.
PIP_INDEX_URL=https://pypi.org/simple/
# PIP_EXTRA_INDEX_URL=
# PIP_TRUSTED_HOST=
# NPM_CONFIG_REGISTRY=https://registry.npmmirror.com
# Docker-in-Docker registry mirrors for scripts/dind-run.sh.
# Use comma-separated values when multiple mirrors are available.
DIND_REGISTRY_MIRRORS=https://docker.m.daocloud.io,https://mirror.ccs.tencentyun.com
# Docker-in-Docker default address pools for nested bridge networks.
# Semicolon-separated multiple Docker daemon pool specs when needed.
DIND_DEFAULT_ADDRESS_POOLS=base=10.200.0.0/13,size=21
GO111MODULE=on
GOPROXY=https://goproxy.cn,direct
GOSUMDB=sum.golang.google.cn
RUSTUP_UPDATE_ROOT=https://mirrors.tuna.tsinghua.edu.cn/rustup/rustup
RUSTUP_DIST_SERVER=https://mirrors.tuna.tsinghua.edu.cn/rustup
CARGO_REGISTRY_REPLACE_WITH=mirror
CARGO_REGISTRY_URL=sparse+https://mirrors.tuna.tsinghua.edu.cn/crates.io-index/
